Particle prep without the per-particle setup (src_acc_tt/tt_prep.h), and a recorder of its inputs and outputs.

Applies on top of relion5-tt.patch and relion5-estep-profile.patch. One file changes. In
getFourierTransformsAndCtfs the common case (2D, even square box, --zero_mask, no helix, no separate
reconstruction images) runs TTPrep: the same norm correction, whole-pixel shift, two FFTs, soft mask,
window and power sums, with the mask weights, shell indices and FFT plans kept across particles and no
per-particle allocation. With --preread_images it reads the stored single-precision image directly, so the
double-precision copy of the box that RELION allocates and fills per particle is not made. Any other case
runs RELION's code unchanged; TT_RELION_PREP=0 forces that.
The mask radius moves up a few lines so both paths and the multibody code after them see it.
The CTF image of a plain optics group (no magnification matrix, no even Zernike offset, no CTF padding) comes
from TTPrep::ctf: the same phase expressions, the sin of a row at a time from glibc's vector library.
TT_RELION_RECORD_PREP=<dir> writes a particle's inputs and the five outputs of either path.

